#### Query 5 — Análisis geográfico

**Pregunta:** ¿En qué mercados geográficos se concentran los clientes y el revenue?

##### Versión original — Solo volumen

sql

```sql
SELECT COUNT(o.order_id) AS cantidad, o.product_id, p.name, p.category, u.country
FROM `projecto-curseradata.case_study.order_items` o
INNER JOIN `projecto-curseradata.case_study.products` p ON o.product_id = p.id
INNER JOIN `projecto-curseradata.case_study.orders` orden ON o.order_id = orden.order_id
INNER JOIN `projecto-curseradata.case_study.users` u ON u.id = o.user_id
WHERE orden.status = 'Complete'
  AND orden.created_at >= '2024-01-01'
GROUP BY o.product_id, p.name, p.category, u.country
HAVING COUNT(o.order_id) >= 4;
```

> ⚠️ **Limitación identificada:** La conclusión sobre China se basó en volumen, no en revenue.

##### Revenue y ticket promedio por país ✅

sql

```sql
SELECT u.country, SUM(o.sale_price) AS total, AVG(o.sale_price) AS promedio, COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS cantidad
FROM `projecto-curseradata.case_study.order_items` o
INNER JOIN `projecto-curseradata.case_study.users` u ON o.user_id = u.id
WHERE o.status = 'Complete'
AND o.created_at >= '2024-01-01'
GROUP BY u.country
ORDER BY total DESC;
```

**Hallazgo:** China es el mayor mercado en revenue total. Sin embargo, varios países del top 10 presentan ticket promedio mayor: Australia (65.26), United Kingdom (64.67), South Korea (60.82), Spain (60.53), Brasil (60.22), France (59.92). Conclusión: volumen alto no equivale a mayor rentabilidad por cliente.

